---
// Week 3 "See It": a qualitative single-coil versus humbucker comparison —
// one coil versus two coils wound in opposition, so external interference
// picked up equally by both cancels while the string signal (which each
// coil senses in a way that combines constructively) does not. No wiring
// detail beyond that broad principle, per CLAUDE.md's "avoid unnecessarily
// detailed wiring configurations."
---

<div class="coil-diagrams">
  <figure class="coil-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 140 80" role="img" aria-label="A single-coil pickup: one coil, one pole-piece row, exposed to external electromagnetic interference with nothing to cancel it.">
      <rect x="35" y="20" width="70" height="34" rx="6" class="coil" />
      <path d="M 42 20 L 42 54 M 50 20 L 50 54 M 96 20 L 96 54 M 104 20 L 104 54" class="coil-hatch" />
      <path d="M 10 10 L 20 16 L 10 22" class="hum-arrow" fill="none" />
      <text x="8" y="8" class="part-label">hum</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="coil-label">Single-coil</span>
      <span class="coil-description">One coil senses the string directly, but also has nothing to cancel electromagnetic interference from nearby equipment — the source of its characteristic hum susceptibility.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure class="coil-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 140 80" role="img" aria-label="A humbucker: two coils wound in opposite polarity, so interference picked up equally by both coils cancels while the string signal does not.">
      <rect x="16" y="20" width="50" height="34" rx="6" class="coil" />
      <path d="M 22 20 L 22 54 M 28 20 L 28 54 M 54 20 L 54 54 M 60 20 L 60 54" class="coil-hatch" />
      <rect x="74" y="20" width="50" height="34" rx="6" class="coil coil--reverse" />
      <path d="M 80 20 L 80 54 M 86 20 L 86 54 M 112 20 L 112 54 M 118 20 L 118 54" class="coil-hatch coil-hatch--reverse" />
      <path d="M 10 10 L 20 16 L 10 22" class="hum-arrow" fill="none" />
      <path d="M 130 10 L 120 16 L 130 22" class="hum-arrow" fill="none" />
      <text x="6" y="8" class="part-label">hum</text>
      <text x="120" y="8" class="part-label">hum</text>
      <text x="70" y="70" class="part-label" text-anchor="middle">opposite winding + polarity</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="coil-label">Humbucker</span>
      <span class="coil-description">Two coils wound in opposite directions with opposite magnetic polarity: interference reaching both coils equally cancels out, while each coil's response to the string combines instead of cancelling.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<style>
  .coil-diagrams {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .coil-card {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .coil-card svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .coil {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--at-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .coil--reverse {
    stroke: var(--bench-phosphor, var(--at-accent));
  }

  .coil-hatch {
    stroke: var(--at-accent);
    stroke-width: 1;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .coil-hatch--reverse {
    stroke: var(--bench-phosphor, var(--at-accent));
  }

  .hum-arrow {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 2 2;
  }

  .part-label {
    font-family: var(--bench-readout, var(--at-font-mono));
    font-size: 6px;
    fill: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .coil-label {
    font-family: var(--bench-readout, var(--at-font-mono));
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--at-text);
  }

  .coil-description {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-xs);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
</style>
